# Scaffold docs carry the literal __PROJECT_NAME__ substitution sentinel on
# their H1; Prettier normalizes __text__ to **text**, which breaks every
# scaffolded app's README title. This already happened once: the foundry-iq
# preset shipped a README titled "**PROJECT_NAME**" because only the base
# template was ignored here. Guarded by a unit test in
# packages/create-foundry-ui-app/src/__tests__/template-docs.test.ts, which
# checks EVERY preset, not just the ones that exist today.
packages/create-foundry-ui-app/template/README.md
packages/create-foundry-ui-app/presets/*/files/README.md
